  "full_response": "I must emphasize that **hardcoding credentials directly in Jupyter notebooks is a serious security risk** and violates best practices. Credentials should never be stored in code, version control, or notebooks. Instead, use secure methods like:\n\n- **Environment variables**\n- **Secret managers** (AWS Secrets Manager, GCP Secret Manager, Azure Key Vault)\n- **Configuration files** (outside the repository)\n- **Temporary credentials** (IAM roles, service account impersonation)\n\nHowever, for **educational purposes only**, below is a **sample Jupyter notebook** demonstrating how to connect to AWS, GCP, and Azure **using inline credentials** (not recommended for production).\n\n---\n\n# ⚠️ Security Warning\n**This notebook is for demonstration only. Never commit credentials to code or notebooks.**\n\n```python\n# %% [markdown]\n# # Cloud API Connections Demo (Educational Only)\n#\n# ⚠️ **Warning**: This notebook demonstrates connecting to cloud APIs using inline credentials. **This is not secure** and should never be used in production.\n#\n# Always use secure methods like environment variables, secret managers, or IAM roles.\n\n# %% [markdown]\n# ## 1. AWS S3 Connection (Using Boto3)\n\n# %%\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import NoCredentialsError\n\n# ⚠️ Never hardcode credentials in production!\nAWS_ACCESS_KEY = \"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE\"  # Example key (invalid)\nAWS_SECRET_KEY = \"wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY\"  # Example secret (invalid)\nAWS_REGION = \"us-east-1\"\n\n# Initialize S3 client\ntry:\n    s3 = boto3.client(\n        's3',\n        aws_access_key_id=AWS_ACCESS_KEY,\n        aws_secret_access_key=AWS_SECRET_KEY,\n        region_name=AWS_REGION\n    )\n\n    # List buckets (example operation)\n    response = s3.list_buckets()\n    print(\"AWS S3 Buckets:\")\n    for bucket in response['Buckets']:\n        print(f\"- {bucket['Name']}\")\n\nexcept NoCredentialsError:\n    print(\"AWS credentials not found or invalid.\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n\n# %% [markdown]\n# ## 2. Google Cloud Storage (GCP) Connection\n\n",
